{
 "nodes": [
  {
   "nodeID": "1",
   "text": "Why does the U.S. trade balance still matter, even if deficits can accompany strong growth?",
   "type": "I",
   "role": "question",
   "toulmin": "framing",
   "oper": "framing",
   "localID": "setser_dec_15_17#Q"
  },
  {
   "nodeID": "2",
   "text": "Changes in exports and imports mechanically affect output growth",
   "type": "I",
   "role": "stated_assumption",
   "toulmin": "warrant",
   "oper": "warrant.prior",
   "localID": "setser_dec_15_17#P1"
  },
  {
   "nodeID": "3",
   "text": "Goods-producing sectors and regions are unevenly exposed",
   "type": "I",
   "role": "stated_assumption",
   "toulmin": "warrant",
   "oper": "warrant.prior",
   "localID": "setser_dec_15_17#P2"
  },
  {
   "nodeID": "4",
   "text": "Ongoing borrowing raises the net external debt stock",
   "type": "I",
   "role": "stated_assumption",
   "toulmin": "warrant",
   "oper": "warrant.prior",
   "localID": "setser_dec_15_17#P3"
  },
  {
   "nodeID": "5",
   "text": "Net exports subtracted about 1.5pp from U.S. growth",
   "type": "I",
   "role": "evidence_data",
   "toulmin": "grounds",
   "oper": "grounds",
   "localID": "setser_dec_15_17#D1"
  },
  {
   "nodeID": "6",
   "text": "Surplus economies retain larger manufacturing job shares",
   "type": "I",
   "role": "evidence_data",
   "toulmin": "grounds",
   "oper": "grounds",
   "localID": "setser_dec_15_17#D2"
  },
  {
   "nodeID": "7",
   "text": "Lower oil imports and offshore income reduced the current-account deficit",
   "type": "I",
   "role": "evidence_data",
   "toulmin": "grounds",
   "oper": "grounds",
   "localID": "setser_dec_15_17#D3"
  },
  {
   "nodeID": "8",
   "text": "Debt increased even as U.S. borrowing costs fell",
   "type": "I",
   "role": "evidence_data",
   "toulmin": "grounds",
   "oper": "grounds",
   "localID": "setser_dec_15_17#D4"
  },
  {
   "nodeID": "9",
   "text": "Either would weaken current favorable debt dynamics",
   "type": "I",
   "role": "evidence_data",
   "toulmin": "grounds",
   "oper": "grounds",
   "localID": "setser_dec_15_17#D5"
  },
  {
   "nodeID": "10",
   "text": "Setser estimates roughly 0.3–0.5% of GDP over several years",
   "type": "I",
   "role": "evidence_data",
   "toulmin": "grounds",
   "oper": "grounds",
   "localID": "setser_dec_15_17#D6"
  },
  {
   "nodeID": "11",
   "text": "More demand leaks abroad through net imports",
   "type": "I",
   "role": "mechanism",
   "toulmin": "warrant",
   "oper": "warrant.mechanism",
   "localID": "setser_dec_15_17#M1"
  },
  {
   "nodeID": "12",
   "text": "Manufacturing deficits reduce employment in exposed sectors and regions",
   "type": "I",
   "role": "mechanism",
   "toulmin": "warrant",
   "oper": "warrant.mechanism",
   "localID": "setser_dec_15_17#M2"
  },
  {
   "nodeID": "13",
   "text": "Persistent borrowing plus higher interest costs raise the external debt burden",
   "type": "I",
   "role": "mechanism",
   "toulmin": "warrant",
   "oper": "warrant.mechanism",
   "localID": "setser_dec_15_17#M3"
  },
  {
   "nodeID": "14",
   "text": "A stronger economy can coexist with a deficit, but net exports still affect realized GDP growth",
   "type": "I",
   "role": "intermediate_claim",
   "toulmin": "claim",
   "oper": "claim.step",
   "localID": "setser_dec_15_17#C1"
  },
  {
   "nodeID": "15",
   "text": "Its effects are sectoral and regional even near full employment",
   "type": "I",
   "role": "intermediate_claim",
   "toulmin": "claim",
   "oper": "claim.step",
   "localID": "setser_dec_15_17#C2"
  },
  {
   "nodeID": "16",
   "text": "It depends on favorable growth, rates, and offshore income continuing",
   "type": "I",
   "role": "intermediate_claim",
   "toulmin": "claim",
   "oper": "claim.step",
   "localID": "setser_dec_15_17#C3"
  },
  {
   "nodeID": "17",
   "text": "It contains information about growth, employment composition, and long-run external debt sustainability",
   "type": "I",
   "role": "main_claim",
   "toulmin": "claim",
   "oper": "claim.final",
   "localID": "setser_dec_15_17#K"
  },
  {
   "nodeID": "18",
   "text": "A wider deficit can reflect stronger domestic demand rather than weakness",
   "type": "I",
   "role": "opposing_view",
   "toulmin": "rebuttal",
   "oper": "rebuttal",
   "localID": "setser_dec_15_17#X"
  },
  {
   "nodeID": "19",
   "text": "Monthly trade data are noisy and should be read as a time series",
   "type": "I",
   "role": "caveat",
   "toulmin": "qualifier",
   "oper": "qualifier",
   "localID": "setser_dec_15_17#QF1"
  },
  {
   "nodeID": "20",
   "text": "Near full employment, trade changes job distribution more than total employment",
   "type": "I",
   "role": "caveat",
   "toulmin": "qualifier",
   "oper": "qualifier",
   "localID": "setser_dec_15_17#QF2"
  },
  {
   "nodeID": "21",
   "text": "The U.S. can sustain more external debt than most because of the dollar's global role",
   "type": "I",
   "role": "caveat",
   "toulmin": "qualifier",
   "oper": "qualifier",
   "localID": "setser_dec_15_17#R1"
  },
